  "section_notes": "S1 is strict with 24-hour serious reporting and 5-business-day other reporting, and no phase-in. S2 keeps a 55°C test and a 5% corrective-action threshold but allows sales above it, so it is weakened despite customer disclosure. S3 sets a 12-month new-unit deadline and a 6-year retrofit window with an alternative for infeasible units. S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months. S5 has a discretionary recall: exceeding 8/100k triggers regulator review and corrective action, but recall only if the regulator finds unacceptable risk."
